# Citation metadata for lsdviztools3 (Citation File Format,
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitHub shows it as "Cite this
# repository"; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
#
# Deliberately no `version:` or `date-released:`. The version lives in
# pyproject.toml and lsdviztools3/__init__.py, and a copy here would go stale;
# Zenodo takes the version and date from the release tag.
#
# Once Zenodo has archived the first release, add its CONCEPT DOI (the one that
# always resolves to the latest version) under identifiers:, e.g.
#
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#       description: Concept DOI, all versions of lsdviztools3
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lsdviztools3 in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "lsdviztools3: visualisation tools for LSDTopoTools3"
abstract: >-
  lsdviztools3 is a Python package for making publication-ready maps and charts
  from the output of LSDTopoTools3 (lsdtt3) and other geographic data: shaded
  relief, channel networks, basins, chi profiles, swath profiles, valley and
  hillslope analyses, landscape evolution model animations and cosmogenic
  nuclide comparisons. Maps are drawn with PyGMT and x-y charts with
  matplotlib. It also wraps the lsdtt3 command-line tools so analyses can be
  run from Python and notebooks.
authors:
